    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n*** This is an over 55's only development ******\n\nApartment 16 Maryland House is a neatly presented two-bedroom apartment located on the garden level of this attractive Georgian property which was cleverly developed in the late 1990's into one and two bedroom apartments. The apartment benefits from having a wraparound open patio immediately outside which is accessible via a door from the living room and benefits from a south/west facing orientation; a most convenient location within a short walk of Shankill Village, the Beach, DART station, the Lidl supermarket complex and a selection of other local services & amenities.\n\nSet on landscaped grounds, Maryland House is a private complex of apartments and bungalows. Accessible via the lift or staircase from the main House entrance (using the main steps or its wheelchair ramp); one can also access the apartment from its own outside entrance, down a short flight of steps under cover and into the living room through a patio door. Internally the bright and spacious accommodation is presented in a good condition throughout. \n\nIn brief, the L-shaped layout comprises an entrance hallway with high ceilings and coving along with a large storage/cloakroom, and a hot-press. Straight in from the front door along the hall is the impressive open plan kitchen/dining/living room featuring ceiling coving, laminate flooring, an electric fireplace, and a door which leads to the paved open patio area outside offering an alternative access point and somewhere to sit and enjoy on a nice day. The galley style kitchen is neatly tucked away next to the dining area but out of sight from the living space and comes fully equipped with plenty of storage. Further along the hallway is the main bedroom with carpet flooring, built in wardrobes and ensuite shower room. Next door is another double bedroom also with carpet flooring and built in wardrobes each bedroom has a large window which provides plenty of natural light. At the end of the hallway is the main bathroom suite. \n\nExternally, this well managed development is enhanced by maintained communal lawns with an array of colourful plants and shrubbery, extensive communal patio area for the use of the residents. In addition, there is also ample surface level parking spaces (unallocated) for the residents and communal bins. \n\nThe location is simply superb, the development is a light stroll from local shops and eateries in Shankill Village, Shankill Beach, and in the immediate vicinity there is the Lidl supermarket complex with a café and a pharmacy, St Anne's Church. Shankill is also well catered for in terms of public transport with regular DART and Dublin Bus routes passing through the village, whilst the Luas at either Cherrywood Carrickmines park & ride is a short distance away."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nLiving / Dining Room - 5.23m x 4.07m\n\n\nKitchen - 2.32m x 2.08m\n\n\nHallway - 3.87m x 8.89m\n\n\nBedroom 1 - 5.54m x 4.14m\n\n\nEnsuite - 2.11m x 1.82m\n\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.14m x 4.90m\n\n\nBathroom - 1.65m x 2.63m\n\n\n"
